content:
Evidence from the datasheet: the only multi-valued parameters that co-occur on the same table rows are the two **Transmitter Optical Characteristics** rows (fiber type with **Output Optical Power** minimum). **100BASE-FX** and **IEEE 802.3u** describe one interface (Features). **Power dissipation** values sit in separate Transmitter vs Receiver electrical tables (typ/max), not on the fiber rows, so they are not assigned to fiber modes.

```json
{
  "modes": [
    {
      "label": "62.5/125 µm multimode (NA 0.275)",
      "standards_code": "100BASE-FX",
      "tx_power_min_dbm": -20.0
    },
    {
      "label": "50/125 µm multimode (NA 0.20)",
      "standards_code": "100BASE-FX",
      "tx_power_min_dbm": -23.5
    }
  ]
}
```
